## 6. Kill-conditions (what would re-open the route)

- **If `dim F ≠ card − C − δ` for some `(d, r)`** — refuted: exact Singular Krull dim matches in all 13
  cases (N=2,3; symmetric/asymmetric; all r). The fibration count `(card−C)−δ` reproduces every row.
- **If `mult|_{Σ̄^r} → Mat^{≤r}` were not dominant** (so the generic-fibre count fails) — would break §3.
  Guarded by `r ≤ min_i d_i` (then `E` is realisable as a product and the rank-`r` stratum is hit).
  Codex flagged this as the needed hypothesis; it is exactly the realizability requirement.
- **If the top component were everywhere non-reduced / singular** (tangent strictly bigger than dim) —
  then `rank < C+δ` generically and `dim F` would read too big. Refuted indirectly: Singular `dim F`
  already equals `card − C − δ` (the *variety* dimension, radical-insensitive), and char-0 generic
  smoothness gives a reduced generic point on each component. H3c needs *generic reducedness* of the
  top component only (NOT global reducedness — that was the thread-20 wall, off this path).

## 7. Caveats

- `C` is read on `sorted d` (permutation invariance of `(C, θ)`, LANDED). `(1,2,1)`, `(3,2,3)` etc.
  are non-monotone; the `cValue` closed form requires monotone input, so sort first.
- The "generic point" is generic *on the top component*, NOT on `Rep_d` and NOT the max-rank fibre
  point. The recurring trap (lower-semicontinuity): maximizing Jacobian rank over the whole fibre
  picks up a *lower*-dimensional submersion component and reports `d_N d_0`, not `C+δ`.
